                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d2edcdb-99c5-347f-9e28-d5c507bcbd2e",
                        "entry_id": "a699c683-09ee-345c-97d6-6be782c82c64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. смесь чего-либо разнородного"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "820b6396-431e-4034-b512-daaa667ca828",
                                "sense_id": "4d2edcdb-99c5-347f-9e28-d5c507bcbd2e",
                                "text": "Разговаривали мы на языковой мешанине, потому что Вильнюс – город абсолютно нелитовский."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29b11e89-b364-42b9-b58f-ccea2b8b56c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "a699c683-09ee-345c-97d6-6be782c82c64",
                        "source_sense_id": "4d2edcdb-99c5-347f-9e28-d5c507bcbd2e",
                        "target_lang_word": "medley",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "medley",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9288f05-a18f-3849-821f-96654b2d1dbb",
                                        "entry_id": "da19b054-133c-3894-b7ac-66538ed0d313",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Combat, fighting; a battle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80ce10a2-1df1-485e-ad34-db47535b7c8f",
                                                "sense_id": "e9288f05-a18f-3849-821f-96654b2d1dbb",
                                                "text": "Thenne came the kyng of Irland and the kynge of the stryete marches to rescowe syre Tristram and sire Palomydes / There beganne a grete medle / & many knyghtes were smyten doune on bothe partyes / and alweyes sir launcelot spared sir Tristram / and he spared hym"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d619dd41-ae51-4c62-81b5-586a6383a373",
                                                "sense_id": "e9288f05-a18f-3849-821f-96654b2d1dbb",
                                                "text": "For greater shields they have, than that they can either doe or see ought, and being raunged by hundreds no doubt they will hinder one another in the medley, except some very few"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcdb60e6-918c-300b-b4b9-774c3cf31155",
                                        "entry_id": "da19b054-133c-3894-b7ac-66538ed0d313",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection or mixture of miscellaneous things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b05c7ba-8ea9-475c-854f-f73e241871a7",
                                                "sense_id": "bcdb60e6-918c-300b-b4b9-774c3cf31155",
                                                "text": "a fruit medley"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ac8abb1-f997-4890-a90a-50f03e9a5241",
                                                "sense_id": "bcdb60e6-918c-300b-b4b9-774c3cf31155",
                                                "text": "this medley of philosophy and war"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78882b93-9780-46bd-8bca-bfabb4bee1c5",
                                                "sense_id": "bcdb60e6-918c-300b-b4b9-774c3cf31155",
                                                "text": "Love is a medley of endearments, jars, / Suspicions, reconcilements, wars."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "200c5543-7b08-3b46-b9f3-6084e946aeff",
                                        "entry_id": "da19b054-133c-3894-b7ac-66538ed0d313",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection of related songs played or mixed together as a single piece."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9f6135e-3994-4fdc-bfd8-76f2d81a826d",
                                                "sense_id": "200c5543-7b08-3b46-b9f3-6084e946aeff",
                                                "text": "They played a medley of favorite folk songs as an encore."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3800f507-9775-35e1-b828-df53b6363cd6",
                                        "entry_id": "da19b054-133c-3894-b7ac-66538ed0d313",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A competitive swimming event that combines the four strokes of butterfly, backstroke, breaststroke, and freestyle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de190ad8-d59e-384b-8412-3f49dbeaf9c5",
                                        "entry_id": "da19b054-133c-3894-b7ac-66538ed0d313",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cloth of mixed colours."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9f808ab-94ee-4cb0-bd2e-9d6270569d17",
                                                "sense_id": "de190ad8-d59e-384b-8412-3f49dbeaf9c5",
                                                "text": "Otherwise , as our Saviour noteth , when the old Cloth was joyned to the new , it made no good medley , but the Rent was made the wors"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "medley",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d08dcf28-2514-37d0-92dd-c6c3ea0f37ef",
                                        "entry_id": "fee0382d-5092-32c3-b9fc-4a2f4f523ac8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To combine, to form a medley."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5742bd86-8aa3-43c1-b9cd-fb65c26feb35",
                        "source_entry_id": "a699c683-09ee-345c-97d6-6be782c82c64",
                        "source_sense_id": "4d2edcdb-99c5-347f-9e28-d5c507bcbd2e",
                        "target_lang_word": "jumble",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jumble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "652648bd-91a5-3d81-ab4b-75c6f7e1fea3",
                                        "entry_id": "c38e75a7-467f-31c1-b458-c2849f4c5616",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mix or confuse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "662c077f-0a3e-493b-83c1-de6c06a4c186",
                                                "sense_id": "652648bd-91a5-3d81-ab4b-75c6f7e1fea3",
                                                "text": "Every clime and age jumbled together."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b6eaa95-a8ce-4a63-95da-8c9794231612",
                                                "sense_id": "652648bd-91a5-3d81-ab4b-75c6f7e1fea3",
                                                "text": "Why dost thou blend and jumble such inconsistencies together?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69ac2908-a39e-31ca-b255-0b0ceaefcc84",
                                        "entry_id": "c38e75a7-467f-31c1-b458-c2849f4c5616",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To meet or unite in a confused way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eadd70f1-70d6-4c6d-9810-16e1c5838e17",
                                                "sense_id": "69ac2908-a39e-31ca-b255-0b0ceaefcc84",
                                                "text": "I tried to study, but in my half-awake state, all of the concepts seemed to jumble together."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "jumble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9767489-edff-34ed-bb12-6af357074ab8",
                                        "entry_id": "6053e1cc-1ada-356b-8ea0-3766467aa3b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mixture of often unrelated things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2bc34f3-92ce-48c9-8e20-5bceeb771255",
                                                "sense_id": "d9767489-edff-34ed-bb12-6af357074ab8",
                                                "text": "His voice was rich and mellow and he had so long been thoroughly persuaded of the weight and import to mankind of any word he said that his words really had come to sound as if there were something in them. But now he can only whisper, and what he whispers sounds like what it is—mere jumble and jargon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c706d811-ffce-49fc-be21-74a27f28b16c",
                                                "sense_id": "d9767489-edff-34ed-bb12-6af357074ab8",
                                                "text": "The bufferbeam is another factor that must be carefully considered. The buffing and coupling centre is 3ft 5½in above rail level and the beam carries not only buffers and drawgear but a jumble of train connections such as jumpers and pipes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecabfbdd-13b6-4dae-b3d8-194d6146cc51",
                                                "sense_id": "d9767489-edff-34ed-bb12-6af357074ab8",
                                                "text": "The newspaper letters, all capitals, made up a jumble of typefaces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e16654a-0119-3c07-9447-a1020d22c44e",
                                        "entry_id": "6053e1cc-1ada-356b-8ea0-3766467aa3b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Items for a rummage sale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8159b233-103a-4ecf-b72e-fa38368c6d57",
                                                "sense_id": "9e16654a-0119-3c07-9447-a1020d22c44e",
                                                "text": "Hire a stall at a fair or sell your wares at a car boot sale. Adjust your jumble's price to something very reasonable and attractive for people to buy. Your income will depend on the quality and quantity of the jumble […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
